// Curation list for scripts/fetch_corpus.py import-hb-tests --curated; see
// `about` and docs/conformance.adoc. --pin-fonts rewrites this file in
// canonical form (this header kept, other comments dropped): put
// explanations in `reason`.
{
  "about": "HarfBuzz shaping-test cases curated into roc-font's own case files (architecture §7.1, docs/conformance.adoc). Each entry names one case by suite, upstream file and line in the pinned HarfBuzz release, plus `case`, the first 16 hex digits of the SHA-256 of the normalised line (fields stripped, whitespace collapsed), so a case that moved between versions is still found. `gating: true` entries go to tests/cases/hb-curated/<suite>.jsonc and must agree; the rest go to tests/cases/hb-pending/<milestone>.jsonc, a scored suite. `milestone` is the TODO.md milestone expected to make the case pass (M1-now: passes today; M1-next: lands with work in progress; post-0.1: after 0.1.0), `needs` the capabilities still missing, `reason` why the case is in scope. `fonts` pins every font used (SHA-256 and size); fonts up to font_size_cap bytes are copied into tests/cases/hb-fonts/. Run `python3 scripts/fetch_corpus.py import-hb-tests --curated` after editing; promote a case by setting gating to true.",
  "schema": 1,
  "source": {
    "corpus": "harfbuzz-14.6.0",
    "path": "test/shape/data"
  },
